comment_data.body:
@mstinsky, thanks to a series of refactors and optimizations (see [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1007#issuecomment-2252493138) if you are curious which ones), this is now possible on latest `main` with a few necessary setup tweaks. Here is a setup that makes it work:

```lua
local ext_skip = { yml = true }
require('mini.icons').setup({
  use_file_extension = function(ext, _) return not ext_skip[ext:lower()] end,
})
```

This setup basically tells 'mini.icons' that 'yml' filetype should be ignored during "file" resolution which results in always relying on `vim.filetype.match()` output (which is essentially what is needed here). See [help entry](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/fb2cbeb4bff225e3c7907cfcd95ebf2a4492f8b6/doc/mini-icons.txt#L237) for more details.

Assuming the `vim.filetype.add({ pattern = { ['.*/roles/.*/tasks/.*%.ya?ml'] = 'yaml.ansible' } })` filetype detection set up, here is how it looks in latest 'mini.files':

![screenshot_2024-07-26_13:48:39](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a6fee5c-bf9c-4a65-998f-705f3efef439)

Note that this requires that `MiniIcons.get('file', ...)` is called with a string that satisfies the pattern matching rules, which is usually a full path. So this might not work if 'mini.icons' user (usually plugin) calls it only with basename.

------

This question/issue was the main driving force for making those (overall positive) changes happen, so thanks for creating it!

